e036dd6f-dba1-42b4-a47f-55d8b512935c	\N	Deep-init docs suite - Axi app projects batch	Use the deep-init-pro documentation standard, but do not rely on loading a skill file at runtime. First explore the assigned project paths, then generate or update their root documentation suites.\n\nAssigned write scope:\n- /Volumes/code/workspace/projects/axi-notify\n- /Volumes/code/workspace/projects/axi-image-preview\n- /Volumes/code/workspace/projects/axi-pet\n- /Volumes/code/workspace/projects/axi-docs\n\nRequired docs per assigned project root:\nREADME.md, README.zh-CN.md, AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG.md, TODO.md, MILESTONES.md, INDEX.md, PRD.md, TDD.md\n\nDocument meaning:\n- README.md: concise English project entrypoint, purpose, layout, run/verify commands.\n- README.zh-CN.md: concise Simplified Chinese counterpart.\n- AGENTS.md: root agent rules, boundaries, verification, and local doc read order.\n- CHANGELOG.md: Keep-a-Changelog style, starting with an Unreleased section.\n- TODO.md: P0/P1/P2 tasks with requirement IDs; P0/P1 include test cases.\n- MILESTONES.md: evidence-backed milestones and current status.\n- INDEX.md: document map and ownership/source-of-truth index.\n- PRD.md: product/project requirements, users, acceptance criteria, non-goals.\n- TDD.md: test/technical design document covering architecture assumptions, test strategy, verification commands, and risk cases.\n\nRules:\n- Read /Volumes/code/workspace/AGENTS.md and each project-local AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md/README/package manifest before writing.\n- Preserve human-authored content, especially anything after <!-- MANUAL -->. If a required file exists, improve it incrementally instead of replacing it wholesale.\n- Do not edit files outside the assigned write scope.\n- For third-party/reference repos, make docs explicitly local-overlay/reference governance docs; do not claim Axi owns upstream product direction.\n- Prefer accurate, short, professional docs over template filler.\n- Every P0/P1 TODO item must include a